; Stage 15 W8 G-4: this fixture pins a KNOWN GAP, not an intended feature.
;
; `g4-lc-dst`'s initializer reads `g4-lc-src` — a global whose own `defvar` is
; reached later — but it does so THROUGH A CALL, so no syntactic reference to
; `g4-lc-src` appears in the initializer and the ordering check cannot see it.
; Detecting this needs callee effect summaries, which
; design/stage15-stress-test/nullability.md §9 declares a permanent non-goal,
; and design/global-init.md §4.2 and §6 adopt the same boundary. The compiler's
; own shape, `(vector-new-in (addr-of g-arena-alloc))`, is this case.
;
; So this compiles, and `g4-lc-dst` ends up **0**, not 99. `run_g4_order` links
; and runs it and asserts the observed value: `main` returns `(+ 10 g4-lc-dst)`,
; so the gap reads as exit 10 and a future fix that closed it — either by
; diagnosing the shape or by ordering the initializers — would read as 109 and
; fail loudly here rather than passing quietly.
;
; The directly-spelled version of the same dependency, `(defvar g4-lc-dst:i32
; g4-lc-src)`, IS rejected; see g4-forward-ref.nuc.
(defn g4-lc-seed ():i32 (return 99))
(defn g4-lc-read ():i32 (return g4-lc-src))

(defvar g4-lc-dst:i32 (g4-lc-read))
(defvar g4-lc-src:i32 (g4-lc-seed))

(defn main ():i32 (return (+ 10 g4-lc-dst)))
